 ### [Exponentially Ascending Gradient Threshold](9684-exponentially-ascending-gradient-threshold.md)
-A densification control mechanism that uses an exponentially ascending gradient threshold to regulate splitting and cloning. It allows aggressive densification early in training and restricts it later to prevent overfitting.
+A densification control mechanism that uses an exponentially ascending gradient threshold to regulate splitting and cloning. It solves the trade-off between early-stage convergence speed and late-stage overfitting by allowing aggressive densification when few Gaussians exist and restricting it as the scene becomes dense. It sets itself apart from static threshold methods by dynamically adjusting the sensitivity of densification decisions based on the normalized training progress.
 
 ### [SplatFormer Training Objective & Refinement](11745-splatformer-training-objective-refinement.md)
